Sure thing!
So go into the plugin parameters of
Skill States Core
, click
Skill Cost Types
, and copy the existing entry for MP and paste it at the bottom of the list. Click into it and rename it whatever you want (I'll assume Stamina).
In JS: Draw Gauge, I'd make the following changes:
Spoiler:
JS: Draw Gauge
Code:
// Declare Settings
const color1 = ColorManager.textColor(x);
const color2 = ColorManager.textColor(y);
const label = "SP";

// Declare Variables
const sprite = this;
const settings = sprite._costSettings;
const bitmap = sprite.bitmap;
const user = sprite._battler;
const currentValue = sprite.currentDisplayedValue();
const bitmapWidth = sprite.bitmapWidth();
const bitmapHeight = sprite.textHeight ? sprite.textHeight() : sprite.bitmapHeight();
const gaugeHeight = sprite.gaugeHeight();

// Draw Gauge
const gx = 0;
const gy = bitmapHeight - gaugeHeight;
const gw = bitmapWidth - gx;
const gh = gaugeHeight;
this.drawFullGauge(color1, color2, gx, gy, gw, gh);

// Draw Label
const lx = 4;
const ly = 0;
const lw = bitmapWidth;
const lh = bitmapHeight;
sprite.setupLabelFont();
bitmap.paintOpacity = 255;
bitmap.drawText(label, lx, ly, lw, lh, "left");

// Draw Value
const vw = bitmapWidth - 2;
const vh = bitmapHeight;
sprite.setupValueFont();
bitmap.textColor = ColorManager.mpColor(user);
bitmap.drawText(currentValue, 0, 0, vw, vh, "right");
Again, I assumed you'd want to call it SP for Stamina Points, but you can make the label anything you want. X and Y at the top can either by colors from your window system image, or hex codes -- these determine what color your aliased gauge is going to be.
Now, in the class or actor page for the character, insert this notetag:
<Replace MP Gauge: Stamina> (or whatever you named it to)
Now, your character should I BELIEVE still use skills with MP costs as normal, but to your player it's going to look like his skills cost a different resource. If you want to change how his "SP" cost looks vs MP costs in the menu, like a different color vs MP, you can edit that in the plugin as well. LMK if you need help with that, too.

